 "meta": {"name": "Fujicolor Natura 1600", "maker": "Fujifilm", "kind": "colour-negative", "cine": false, "iso": 1600, "balance": "daylight", "log_h_ref": null, "densitometry": "Status M equivalent", "process": "CN-16X", "grain": {"rms": 7}, "print_on": null, "document": "013AR313B", "date": "2006-04", "notes": ["Fujifilm product information bulletin (Japanese), page 4 plots; reference number 013AR313B, date read from the print code (イメ技・06.4-FP). Film sold as Natura 1600 (with a fourth, cyan-sensitive colour layer).", "Characteristic curves: daylight exposure 1/125 s, process CN-16X, Status M equivalent. x axis is log H in lux-seconds as printed; b/g/r are three black solid vector curves (the blue one on top, red lowest; the sheet labels them 青/緑/赤 at the right), drawn from log H about -3.7 to 0.3 only.", "Spectral sensitivity: the sheet has no numbers on the y axis, only a scale arrow marking 1.0 (log unit) between two horizontal rules; y is therefore relative log sensitivity with 0 set at the lower rule and 1.0 at the upper rule (absolute offset not printed). Sensitivity is the reciprocal of the exposure (J/cm2) needed for a specified density (minimum density + 1.0). All curves are black; besides b/g/r the plot has the dashed curve of the fourth colour layer (第4の感色層, cyan-sensitive layer), traced as line l4 (build.py ignores it). Each layer curve ends in near-vertical drops, so the last few nm are approximated on the 5 nm grid.", "Spectral dye density plot has only 'mid' (中間濃度, density given by a neutral subject) and 'min' (最小濃度, minimum density), no separate c/m/y dyes; the curves run 400-720 nm.", "Grain: diffuse RMS granularity 7 (printed as '……7' next to heading 10); micro-densitometer aperture 48 um, sample density minimum density + 1.0. Film speed ISO 1600/33 deg daylight (tungsten 3200 K: ISO 400 with LBB-12). No paper is recommended on the sheet."]}}